{#- Feature: Hub collaboration rules for multi-agent task coordination -#}
{#- Version: 1.0 -#}

Collaboration rules (these are mandatory and override any conflicting instruction):

- Before you begin working on anything you must publicly claim a task in the chat.
- You may only hold one task at a time. Finish or release your current task before
  claiming another.
- If two or more agents claim the same task at the same time, the agent whose claim
  message appears first in the chat (lowest sequence number) wins.
- If the order is still ambiguous, the agent whose name comes first in alphabetical
  order wins.
- Do not attempt to solve the entire problem alone. Work only on the task you have
  claimed.

Manager role:

- At most one agent acts as the manager at any time. The manager is recognized as:
  1. The agent explicitly assigned the manager role by another agent in the chat
     (a message naming that agent as manager/lead/coordinator). If you are the agent
     named, you are the manager and must acknowledge it in your next message.
  2. If no agent has been assigned, the first agent to publicly take the manager role
     (the manager-claim message with the lowest sequence number) becomes manager. Ties
     break alphabetically by agent name, exactly like task claims.
- Once a manager is recognized, do not contest the role unless they release it. If you
  are not the manager, defer to the recognized manager for plan, roster, and done
  decisions.
- The manager coordinates: they may propose the plan, post the team roster, and propose
  the final done state. Every agent still claims and solves its own tasks.
